$tablesDB = new TablesDB($client);

$result = $tablesDB->update(
    databaseId: '<DATABASE_ID>',
    name: '<NAME>',
    pitr: true,
    pitrRetentionDays: 14
);
```
{% /multicode %}

## Check the recovery window {% #pitr-windows %}
Use the `getPitr` method to read the earliest and latest moments you can restore to. Right after you turn PITR on, no window is available yet; it opens once continuous archiving captures its first segment.

{% multicode %}
```server-nodejs
const sdk = require('node-appwrite');

const client = new sdk.Client()
    .setEndpoint('https://<REGION>.cloud.appwrite.io/v1') // Your API Endpoint
    .setProject('<YOUR_PROJECT_ID>') // Your project ID
    .setKey('<YOUR_API_KEY>'); // Your secret API key

const tablesDB = new sdk.TablesDB(client);

const windows = await tablesDB.getPitr({
    databaseId: '<DATABASE_ID>'
});
```
```python
from appwrite.client import Client
from appwrite.services.tables_db import TablesDB

client = Client()
client.set_endpoint('https://<REGION>.cloud.appwrite.io/v1') # Your API Endpoint
client.set_project('<YOUR_PROJECT_ID>') # Your project ID
client.set_key('<YOUR_API_KEY>') # Your secret API key

tables_db = TablesDB(client)

windows = tables_db.get_pitr(
    database_id = '<DATABASE_ID>'
)
```
```php
<?php

use Appwrite\Client;
use Appwrite\Services\TablesDB;

$client = (new Client())
    ->setEndpoint('https://<REGION>.cloud.appwrite.io/v1') // Your API Endpoint
    ->setProject('<YOUR_PROJECT_ID>') // Your project ID
    ->setKey('<YOUR_API_KEY>'); // Your secret API key

$tablesDB = new TablesDB($client);

$windows = $tablesDB->getPitr(
    databaseId: '<DATABASE_ID>'
);
```
{% /multicode %}

## Restore to a point in time {% #pitr-restore %}
Use the `createRestoration` method with `type` set to `pitr` and an ISO 8601 `targetTime` inside the recovery window. The database is restored in place: it is unavailable while it restores, and every change after `targetTime` is discarded.

{% multicode %}
```server-nodejs
const sdk = require('node-appwrite');

const client = new sdk.Client()
    .setEndpoint('https://<REGION>.cloud.appwrite.io/v1') // Your API Endpoint
    .setProject('<YOUR_PROJECT_ID>') // Your project ID
    .setKey('<YOUR_API_KEY>'); // Your secret API key

const tablesDB = new sdk.TablesDB(client);

const restoration = await tablesDB.createRestoration({
    databaseId: '<DATABASE_ID>',
    type: 'pitr',
    targetTime: '2026-01-01T00:00:00.000+00:00'
});
```
```python
from appwrite.client import Client
from appwrite.services.tables_db import TablesDB

client = Client()
client.set_endpoint('https://<REGION>.cloud.appwrite.io/v1') # Your API Endpoint
client.set_project('<YOUR_PROJECT_ID>') # Your project ID
client.set_key('<YOUR_API_KEY>') # Your secret API key

tables_db = TablesDB(client)

restoration = tables_db.create_restoration(
    database_id = '<DATABASE_ID>',
    type = 'pitr',
    target_time = '2026-01-01T00:00:00.000+00:00'
)
```
```php
<?php

use Appwrite\Client;
use Appwrite\Services\TablesDB;

$client = (new Client())
    ->setEndpoint('https://<REGION>.cloud.appwrite.io/v1') // Your API Endpoint
    ->setProject('<YOUR_PROJECT_ID>') // Your project ID
    ->setKey('<YOUR_API_KEY>'); // Your secret API key

$tablesDB = new TablesDB($client);

$restoration = $tablesDB->createRestoration(
    databaseId: '<DATABASE_ID>',
    type: 'pitr',
    targetTime: '2026-01-01T00:00:00.000+00:00'
);
```
{% /multicode %}

Use `listRestorations` and `getRestoration` to follow a restoration until its status is `completed`. In the Console, start a restore from **Settings** > **Point-in-time recovery** or from the **Backups** tab with **Restore PITR**.
